{"content":[{"c":["SHAVEH KIRIATHAIM*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Plain east of the Dead Sea near the city of Kiriathaim and occupied by the people of Emim. The Emimites in Shaveh Kiriathaim are listed with a number of other tribes and nations that King Kedorlaomer and his allies defeated (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.14.5","r":"Gen.14.5","rawR":"Gen.14.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.14.5","value":"Gen.14.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 14:5"},"; ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},", “Kiriathaim”). This plain was later inherited by the sons of Reuben."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"ShavehKiriathaim","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 14:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.14.5","rawQueryValue":"Gen.14.5","sourceRefExact":"Gen.14.5"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"7f28851b12af77e3d85828886a501d64f0a07d477ab98f84675f30feb8f657cd","sourceItemName":"ShavehKiriathaim","sourceItemOrder":227,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"ShavehKiriathaim","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Shaveh Kiriathaim*","title":"Shaveh Kiriathaim*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}